A '''Youngster''' (Japanese: '''{{tt|たんぱんこぞう|Generation III, V, VI, and IX, SMSUSUM, SwSh}}''' / '''{{tt|たんパンこぞう|Generation I, II, and IV, LGPE, BDSP}}''' ''Shorts Youngster'', shortened in [[Generation I]] to '''たんパン''' ''Shorts'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that debuted in the [[Generation I]] games. They are depicted as average young boys usually wearing caps and short pants.

They use a variety of Pokémon, but they tend to use common ones that are caught early in their respective games. In [[Unova]] and [[Kalos]], a significant amount of Youngsters specialize in {{type|Bug}} Pokémon, likely due to the absence of the {{tc|Bug Catcher}} class in those regions. Some will give out [[Ultra Ball]]s when defeated. In the [[Battle Maison]], they specialize in Bug- and {{type|Normal}} Pokémon.

Youngsters appear to be the male counterparts of {{tc|Lass}}es.

In [[Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!|Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!]], Youngsters will award three {{i|Poké Ball}}s along with [[prize money]] upon being defeated, except for [[Master Trainer]]s.

In [[Pokémon Stadium]], they are referred to as '''Lads'''.

