===={{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}====
{{main|Joey}}

Joey is [[Professor Elm]]'s assistant and his errand boy. His partner {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} is {{p|Rattata}}. In [[Chuang Yi]]'s translations of the manga, he was known as '''Grant'''. However, [[VIZ Media]]'s translations properly identify him as Joey.

===={{MangaArc|Emerald}}====
In ''[[PS337|Epilogue]]'', Joey makes a cameo appearance in one of the ships heading to the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|III}}.

===={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}====
A Youngster is seen amongst the many people visiting the {{safari|Johto}} in ''[[PS446|Weavile Wobbles But It Won't Fall Down]]''.

===={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}====
A Youngster appears in ''[[PS342|A Conk on Cranidos's Cranium]]'', where he serves as {{adv|Platinum}}'s first opponent at the [[Oreburgh Gym]].

[[File:Youngster VI Adventures.png|thumb|120px|left|A Youngster in the {{MangaArc|X & Y}}]]
===={{MangaArc|Platinum}}====
A Youngster appears in ''[[PS426|Softening Up Kakuna]]'' as a challenger of the {{gdis|Battle Factory|IV}}. In the battle shown, he rents a {{p|Gabite}}, {{p|Finneon}}, and Trash Cloak {{p|Wormadam}}, later trading the Wormadam for a {{p|Forretress}}. Another Youngster appeared in ''[[PS421|Clobbering Claydol]]'', wandering around the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}}.

===={{MangaArc|Black & White}}====
A Youngster with a {{p|Woobat}} appeared in ''[[PS466|An Odd Speech]]'', listening to Ghetsis's speech but ultimately disregarding what he said about releasing his Pokémon.

A Youngster with a {{p|Crustle}} is seen in ''[[PS511|Dream a Little Dream]]'' amongst the many Trainers entering {{OBP|Victory Road|Black and White}}.

[[Leo]], a boy wearing a combination of Youngster and {{tc|Poké Maniac}} clothes, appears as a recurring character in both Black & White and {{MangaArc|Black 2 & White 2}}.

===={{MangaArc|X & Y}}====
In ''[[PS549|An X-cuse to Come Out and Play]]'', a Youngster was seen fleeing from a battle between {{p|Xerneas}} and {{p|Yveltal}}.

In ''[[PS553|Sylveon Enchants]]'', a Youngster was seen in the Mini-game Corner with his {{p|Binacle}}.

A Youngster appeared in ''[[PS560|Trevenant Pokes]]'' with his younger brother, a {{tc|Preschooler}}, at the [[Tower of Mastery]] before deciding to go home.

A Youngster appeared in [[Diantha]]'s flashback in ''[[PS582|Pinsir Glares]]''.

===={{MangaArc|Sun, Moon, Ultra Sun & Ultra Moon}}====
In ''[[PASM19|Truth and the Mastermind Behind Team Skull]]'', someone was heard calling for Youngster [[Malie Garden|Tyler]] at [[Hokulani Observatory]].

===={{MangaArc|Sword & Shield}}====
A Youngster with a {{p|Grookey}} appeared in [[Henry Sword]]'s fantasy in ''[[PASS04|Zap!! A Rising Beam of Light]]'', where he explained to [[Casey Shield]] that they would need a nickname for [[Marvin]]'s [[Sniffler|Sobble]] to avoid confusion in case another Trainer had the same Pokémon.

